    "updated_at": "2020-06-15T12:04:43Z",
    "body": "So I think the main thing here is that we added special semantics to `cache.match()` for COEP/CORP to simplify the implementation, but did not do anything for redirects. Meaning the solution to hide redirect secrets would end up being so involved it would never be done. (It was already considered too complex for the more general problem of opaque responses.)\r\n\r\nCould we require the CORP header for redirects you want to store in the cache? Is that too much of a hack?",
